  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The order of basicity is I $>$ III $>$ II $>$ IV The lone pair of electrons on $\\mathrm{N}$ is more readily available for protonation in I and III then in II. III contains an oxygen atom which has - I effect due to which it is less basic than I. In compound IV lone pair of $\\mathrm{e}^{-} \\mathrm{s}$ on $\\mathrm{N}$-atom is contributed towards the aromatic sextet formation and hence is not at all available for protonation. Hence option (b) is correct.",
    "image": null
